      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion, I was thinking to do this in the beginning but I used this approach with parsing stderr because:\n- there are multiple levels of error code remapping in crovm, at least 3 so adding one value in VmEventType would also imply defining there:\n```\nVmEventType::NewResetType\n    -\u003e ExitState::NewResetType \n                        -\u003e CommandStatus::NewResetType -\u003e another remap to an integer))\n```\n- parsing the crosvm `stderr` is not completely different from what we do when we parse string messages from the pipe which is tied to the crosvm serial console\n- parsing the logs can be easily extended with new types",
